- Story & Context: Inside the fermentation shed, Sachi adjusted her gain-pots to mirror the "Koji-Grit"—the proprietary, chaotic language used by radio pirates to describe electromagnetic interference—hoping to hide her illicit broadcast within the humming pulse of the climate-control unit. She stared at the sweating walls of the shed, terrified that her neighbor had finally noticed the unnatural, rhythmic buzzing leaking from the vents. "Align the grain until the pulse forgets its name."
