Track 3: Does The Greenhouse Remember The Sky?
- Story & Context: Decades after the station was dismantled by authorities, botanists at the Conservatory found rare, carnivorous blossoms growing in patterns that perfectly traced the radio waves of the last transmission during the Great Storm of '92. Standing beneath the fractured glass roof as the clouds gathered again, the head researcher finally asked the question that haunted the entire region, watching the petals pulse in rhythm with the thunder. "If the flower blooms, did the signal ever truly cease?"
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A vast, abandoned greenhouse with translucent, vein-covered flowers growing toward an electrical storm visible through a broken dome ceiling.

